# graphify ignore — added 2026-06-14 to cut data/artifact noise from code-graph queries.
# Gitignore-style. Keeps the graph to actual source + specs; drops generated pipeline data.

# Generated pipeline outputs / smoke runs / PDF analyses (pure data, polluted query results)
reports/
**/*_meta.json
**/pdf-analysis.json

# graphify's own output (also auto-skipped, explicit for clarity)
graphify-out/

# vendored skills kit + spec docs (markdown headers were anchoring queries onto non-code)
skills-starter-kit/
**/SKILL.md
DESIGN.md

# old code copies — graphify was indexing backups/ as if live (duplicate generate_pdf nodes)
backups/

# all docs/markdown: keep the graph CODE-only for navigation queries.
# (If wiring graphify↔Smart Connections for a docs+code knowledge graph, drop the lines below.)
docs/
**/*.md

# envs / vendored / build (recursive — backend/.venv was being walked → 128k-node blowup)
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
frontend/build/
frontend/dist/

# generated analysis data (markdown + json per-ticker runs) — pure data, not code
analyses/

# build/deploy output + minified vendor bundles (the REAL node blowup: 108k→~8k)
.vercel/
**/*.min.js
**/*.esm-*.js
**/assets/*.js
**/.next/
**/out/

# caches
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
